            <ArticleTitle>Periorbital pain induced by the concha bullosa fungus ball: a case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>277-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.11607/ofph.1115</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Concha bullosa is characterized by pneumatization of the middle turbinate and is one of the most common variations of the sinonasal anatomy. It is most often asymptomatic. A fungus ball in the concha bullosa is extremely rare, with only two reported cases in the English literature. This article describes a patient with such a fungus ball in the concha bullosa that caused right periorbital pain, specifically in the right medial canthal area, similar to mucosal contact point headache.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
